### AlertIQ 2.0 API - quick test requests
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (humao.rest-client).
### Click "Send Request" above any block below, run top-to-bottom the
### first time so @token gets set from the login response.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### 2. Login (sets @token for the requests below via the response)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=admin&password=ChangeMe123!

### 3. Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 4. List incidents
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 5. Incident stats summary (last 24h)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidents/stats/summary?since_seconds=86400
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 6. List devices
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 7. Engine status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/engine/status
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 8. List demo scenarios
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/demo/scenarios
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 9. Run a demo scenario (creates a REAL incident via the real engine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/demo/simulate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attack_type": "Port Scan"
}

### 10. Get current settings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### 11. Download PDF report (opens/saves in VS Code)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/incidents.pdf?since_seconds=2592000
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
